ally popular in  like the business startup world um  an entrepreneur will like fill out the  lean canvas that's  like a one-page business plan so it goes  through like problem solution like what  you're trying to do so we remixed it and  we took out the parts that were very  like business specific and added things  for open source like contributors and  user profiles  and i think this is really important  because it makes you think about what  you're building the product then also  the community you're trying to build  with it  um yep so you have users and  contributors and i like this green  square for project execution because i  find a lot of people don't think about  the kind of contributors they need in  relation to what they're trying to build  so if you have if you know what your mvp  is your minimum viable product  and what you need for that if you need  designers and a developer you make sure  you put that in your contributors that  you need designers and developers and  then think about how you will onboard  designers if you don't know any  so that's really useful i found and it  helps you write a better readme  if you actually know like your problem  and solution  so that was  i can go back i'm sorry  cool so next one's a road map with  bastion  there's bastion  he's off on the side so  i was really excited um when i paired  bastian with his mentee for this round  because his mentee emailed me back and  was like i can't believe my mentor is  the mark zuckerberg of open source  genetics and he linked me to this  article  and i was like i had no idea  but bastian's pretty cool  he runs opensnip.org  snip is for a single nucleotide  polymorphism which is kind of mutation  you get in  your genome but basically it's um if  you've ever done 23andme or any of those  things that genotypes you you can upload  the results to openstip.org and it's  public and people can use it for  research and you can also match it to  phenotypes so you can see  um yeah what the phenotypes would look  like in use like  it will predict oh you're eastern  european or something like that so oh  fun story um  when bastian uploaded his genotype  before opens he made opensnip um he put  it on github and some random researcher  came along and like analyzed his genome  and then emailed him  and was like hey you have like a higher  likelihood for prostate cancer and  bastian was like oh dear um  but he he was pretty young but he told  his dad and his dad went and got checked  and they caught the cancer early enough  that he was um  yeah he's alive and well now so it's  cool uh you should share your genome  okay  but we helped them through road mapping  oh that's what it was road mapping  even just helping them sort through what  features they wanted over the next few  months and break that down helps them  actually get things done over the next  few months yeah  otherwise  they hadn't been doing a lot for the  year before that so road mapping can  help sort of get your community a  kickstart and help new people come in so  they know what you're working on next  and where they can help  so we have a little like introduction to  road mapping so it helps you break down  milestones and break things down into  issues  yeah  and next on the open source checklist is  a code of conduct where we have richard  this is richard he has a moss beard  um here's another picture of him with no  beard  so richard yeah he's on the left there  this is at mozfest you should all come  to mozfest but  basically oh i didn't make another slide  for him yeah he worked on a lot of  projects this year because he was  actually fellow this past year so one of  the projects he worked on was  slidewinder where he wanted to make  presentations better  so that you can like  remix your html presentations easier  like you can with keynote and stuff  anyways it's cool it's called  slidewinder he wrote a cool code of  conduct for that he was also working on  science fair  which was for li